# nr-office-engine-contracts: the operation contract engine and describe of the office engine (mixdog-office::contracts, mixdog-office::describe), the xlsx validation rule and the docx style definitions (mixdog-office-base)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod capabilities;` add (keep the other modules as they are):

    pub mod contracts;
    pub mod describe;

(the module doc may add: "[`contracts`] checks a batch of operations against the capability tables and rewrites the spellings it accepts in place; [`describe`] answers the `describe` action.")

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-base/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod data_dir;` add:

    pub mod docx_style_defs;

and after `pub mod write_note;` add:

    pub mod xlsx_validation;

(the module doc's list of what the crate holds may add `normalizeXlsxValidation` of `xlsx-contract.mjs` and `docxStyleDefinitions` of `portable-docx-operations.mjs`.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
`[dependencies]`, next to `mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true }`:

    mixdog-office-design = { workspace = true }

(`mixdog-office-design = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-design" }` is already in native/core/Cargo.toml `[workspace.dependencies]`; the crate does not depend on mixdog-office, so there is no cycle.)
Cargo.lock: the `mixdog-office` package's `dependencies` list gains "mixdog-office-design" (alphabetical, after "mixdog-office-base"). No other new edge: mixdog-office-base uses only mixdog-js (JsRegex, js_object_keys, js_to_lowercase, value_to_string), serde_json and its own modules; mixdog-office uses mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-office-design, serde_json and indexmap, which it already has. The twin test uses mixdog-office-base's `twin` (dev-dependency with `test-support`, already present) and `serde_json`.
mixdog-workspace-hack needs no change.

