## compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing: this task registers no protocol method and no service. The engine is a library the office tool's service (a later task of the track) calls: `mixdog_office::contracts::assert_office_operation_contracts(format, backend, &mut operations)` before the backends see a batch, and `mixdog_office::describe::describe_office_capabilities(&DescribeRequest { format, backend, target, operation })` for the `describe` action. The caller maps an extension such as `xlsm` to its format first, as `executeOfficeTool` does.

## Used later (not wired here)
`mixdog_office_base::xlsx_validation::normalize_xlsx_validation` and `mixdog_office_base::docx_style_defs::docx_style_definitions` are what the xlsx and docx engines call; the same code runs in the contract check.
